    "description": "Instruction manual for the local, offline AI assistant on NucleoOS.",
    "details": "NAME\n  anima - NucleoOS Local Offline AI Assistant Guide.\n\nDESCRIPTION\n  ANIMA is the built-in offline assistant for NucleoOS:\n\n  1. LOCAL RETRIEVAL PIPELINE (L0/L1 TIER):\n     - Operates 100% offline on the ESP32S3 hardware. Does not depend on external servers or active internet. No data leaves the device.\n     - The NLP engine normalizes input strings by stripping accents and folding characters to lowercase ASCII.\n     - Computes cosine similarity scores against a pre-compiled semantic index saved on the SD card in '/data/anima/anima-it-index.bin'.\n     - Dialogic Clarify Band: If the best match falls in the uncertainty range [0.50, 0.66) and a second candidate is close, ANIMA prompts the user with a decision ('did you mean 1 or 2?') to prevent wrong assertions or hallucinations.\n\n  2. SUPPORTED COMMANDS & SKILLS:\n     - App Launching: 'open the calculator', 'start notepad', 'show photos'.\n     - System Status: 'what is the battery level', 'what time is it', 'tell me disk space'.\n     - Technical Help: answers queries about ESP32 hardware, electronics, C programming, and OS features.\n     - File Manipulation: 'create a file note.txt' (ANIMA will prompt for options or folder placement).\n\n  3. FROM THE TERMINAL (anima command):\n     SYNOPSIS\n       anima [-o off|on|only] [-l it|en] [-v] [--reset] <question>\n       anima --caps\n       anima --l1 on|off|auto\n     OPTIONS\n       -o off|on|only   Force this turn offline, hybrid, or online-only.\n       -l it|en         Answer language.\n       -v               Add a dim second line with tier, domain, confidence and trace.\n       --reset          Forget the device-side conversation context first.\n       --caps           Print which brain is actually answering: l1 mode, whether it is serving,\n                        whether a teacher key is present and whether online is available.\n       --l1 on|off|auto Pin or free the ~31 KB offline index — the single biggest heap lever\n                        on this chip, and until now buried in a GUI.\n     PIPED INPUT\n       With standard input, anima answers ABOUT the piped text. The firmware's query buffer is\n       160 bytes behind a 208-byte URL buffer, so a 2 KB log cannot be shipped: the browser\n       digests it first — timestamps stripped, distinct lines kept in severity order, duplicates\n       counted — and trims the result to 150 encoded bytes on a code-point boundary. The line\n       actually sent is echoed dimly, so you can see what the brain saw.\n     BEHAVIOUR\n       Down a pipe, anima yields only the reply, and an action is printed rather than performed:\n       a stage that launched an app as a side effect would open windows while writing a file.\n       Run on its own, a launch action reaches the shell. A 503 means another turn holds the\n       brain; it is retried once after the retry_after_ms the device asks for, then reported.\n     DEVICE COST\n       One GET /api/anima per question (two at most, when the brain was busy).\n     EXAMPLES\n       anima \"how much space is left\"\n       dmesg -l E | anima \"what is wrong?\"\n       diag | anima \"is the heap ok?\" | say\n       anima --caps\n       anima --l1 off"
  },
